  "result": "The file is `src/lib/rate-limit.ts`. It holds both things you asked about:\n\n- **How many tries each action gets:** `RATE_LIMIT_BUCKETS` lists a capacity and a refill rate for each kind of action. Password resets are `\"auth:password-reset\": { capacity: 5, refillPerMinute: 1 }`, so five tries, with one more added each minute. Any action not in the list falls back to `DEFAULT_BUCKET`, which is 30 tries refilling at 10 a minute.\n- **Deciding they've run out:** `consumeRateLimit()` tops the bucket back up for the time that has passed, then sets `allowed = tokens >= cost`. It also works out `resetAt`, which is the \"come back later\" time.\n\nThe code that calls it is in `src/actions/auth/reset-password.ts` and `src/server/services/auth-service.ts`. When the check comes back not allowed, those callers only throw `RateLimitedError`; the decision itself isn't made there.\n\nANSWER: src/lib/rate-limit.ts",
